  "problem": "Find $B=\\overset{\u2015}{A}$, where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} & 3-2\\text{i} \\\\ 3-3\\text{i} & 1-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{11}+{b}_{22}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{A} & =\\overset{\u2015}{[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} & 3-2\\text{i} \\\\ 3-3\\text{i} & 1-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{2+4\\text{i}} & \\overset{\u2015}{3-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{3-3\\text{i}} & \\overset{\u2015}{1-5\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-4\\text{i} & 3+2\\text{i} \\\\ 3+3\\text{i} & 1+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{11}+{b}_{22}=(2-4\\text{i})+(1+5\\text{i})=3+\\text{i}.$",
